# Testing is the future / production read-only

Canonical policy: `docs/audits/TESTING_IS_THE_FUTURE_POLICY.md`

## Standing rule

The **testing site** (HDH / `main` testing architecture) is the future of Little Learner Hub.

Build **all** new development, redesigns, bug fixes, curriculum/Teaching Kit work, Family Hub, Forms, Billing (testing), AI, Live→Testing sync, and future features **on testing only**.

**Production is read-only** through all remaining phases until Leah gives **written** approval to deploy.

## Forbidden without written owner approval

- Modify production code directly
- Delete production data
- Overwrite production lesson plans or Teaching Kits
- Publish testing changes to production
- Point production at testing databases or services
- Merge unfinished work into production
- Remove or replace production functionality
- Deploy / merge / publish any production changes

## Live → Testing Feature Sync

Compare production **read-only** to find gaps. Implement only on testing. Never write back to production.

## Before Final QA

Complete `docs/audits/PRE_FINAL_QA_PRODUCTION_UNTOUCHED_AUDIT.md` confirming production untouched, features moved into testing, nothing accidentally lost, and testing is the complete next version.

## Stop rule

If a change could affect production: **stop** and require written approval in the conversation.
